Package: yasmv
Architecture: any
Depends:
 python3 (>= 3.10),
 yasmv-data (= ${source:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Description: SAT-based symbolic model checker for an SMV dialect
 yasmv (Yet Another Symbolic Model Verifier) checks models written in a
 dialect of the SMV language. It decides reachability and invariants
 with bounded model checking, k-induction and interpolation, checks
 guaranteed progress, and simulates models step by step.
 .
 Models can be explored from an interactive shell, through a JSON agent
 protocol, or in a local browser workbench.

Package: yasmv-data
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Recommends:
 yasmv,
Description: SAT-based symbolic model checker for an SMV dialect (data files)
 yasmv (Yet Another Symbolic Model Verifier) checks models written in a
 dialect of the SMV language.
 .
 This package contains the architecture-independent files yasmv needs:
 the arithmetic microcode, the help pages, the JSON schemas, the
 workbench client and the example models.

Package: llvm2smv
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
Recommends:
 clang-18,
 yasmv,
Description: LLVM frontend translating C programs into yasmv models
 llvm2smv reads LLVM 18 IR or bitcode compiled from a supported subset
 of sequential C and translates it into models that yasmv can check.
 Unsupported constructs are rejected with diagnostics.
